# Generated Vite chunks can contain significant whitespace-only lines inside JavaScript
# template literals (for example, indentation in CodeMirror completion snippets).
mcp/src/agents_remember/package_data/dashboard/assets/*.js whitespace=-blank-at-eol

# The vendored tiktoken vocabulary is content-addressed: models/tokens.py checks the
# file's SHA-256 before every load and refuses to start on any copy whose bytes differ. A
# line-ending conversion on a checkout with core.autocrlf=true is exactly that, so without
# this line those clones -- and only those -- cannot start the server at all. Marked binary
# so no EOL or text filter can touch it. Refreshing the vocabulary renames this entry by
# hand. No test checks that the entry names the shipped file, so a forgotten rename shows
# only on a core.autocrlf=true clone. The procedure is in
# mcp/src/agents_remember/package_data/tiktoken/README.md.
mcp/src/agents_remember/package_data/tiktoken/fb374d419588a4632f3f557e76b4b70aebbca790 -text

# The two test-evidence catalogs are lists that every change extends. Git merges them by taking
# both sides' added lines (MIK-R51), so two changes that add a test file no longer stop a sync.
# The union can leave a line twice, a list out of order, or the line of a file that one side
# deleted; both catalog loaders refuse that and name the command that repairs it:
#   python -m agents_remember_test_support.testing.evidence_lifecycle --project-root . --write
mcp/tests/test-evidence-lanes.toml merge=union
mcp/tests/evidence-lifecycle.toml merge=union
